From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:57:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: stop the SIO coprocessor
 window at its mailbox

The T8132 SIO node maps a 0x88000 coprocessor window at 0x3ade00000,
which also covers the SIO's ASC mailbox at 0x3ade08000 (sio_mbox). The
mailbox probes first, so once a board enables the SIO, the SIO driver
cannot request its window and fails with -EBUSY.

Map 0x8000, as T6030 does. The driver only uses the CPU control register
in that window.

Fixes: 6de4b8e4a92a ("arm64: dts: apple: describe disabled T8132 SIO resources")
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi
index b9f37423fb..09861ddb28 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-sio.dtsi
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@
 
 	sio: dma-controller@3ade00000 {
 		compatible = "apple,t8132-sio", "apple,sio";
-		reg = <0x3 0xade00000 0x0 0x88000>,
+		reg = <0x3 0xade00000 0x0 0x8000>,
 		      <0x3 0xad850000 0x0 0x4000>;
 		#dma-cells = <1>;
 		mboxes = <&sio_mbox>;
